## (anonymous) (body-1)

Creates a tab and commands, starts NETWORK_EVENT watching before using blocking APIs, then checks empty/add/add/replace/remove list transitions and destroys commands. It never issues a blocked HTTP request.

- reads: CommandsFactory; resourceCommand; blockedUrls
- writes: Tab, resource listener, observer filter state
- branches: Sequential scenario; assertions compare entire ordered arrays.
- result: Task promise resolves after commands.destroy.
- errors: Assertion/rejection stops task; no local catch or failure-path commands cleanup.
- async: Awaits watcher readiness and each mutation/read.
- ownership: Commands are explicitly destroyed only on normal path; harness owns tab cleanup.

